    "body": "Problem:\nWith `$ALLOW_CONSOLE` set, the winston Console transport writes logs to\nstdout. When stdio is the RPC channel (e.g. remote plugins started by\nNvim), the log lines are read as invalid msgpack-RPC messages, which\nbreaks the channel and kills the host. This reproduces with\n`ALLOW_CONSOLE=1 npm test` in `packages/integration-tests`: the remote\nplugin commands/functions are never registered, so 3 tests fail\n(`E492: Not an editor command: JSHostTestCmd`, `E117: Unknown function: Func`).\n\nSolution:\n- Route all log levels of the Console transport to stderr via\n  `stderrLevels`. stderr is not part of the RPC channel (Nvim collects a\n  job's stderr separately), so `$ALLOW_CONSOLE` is now safe with stdio RPC.\n- Update README and CHANGELOG.\n- Add a test that spawns a process with `ALLOW_CONSOLE=1` and checks that\n  logs (including the patched `console.log`) go to stderr and nothing to stdout.\n\nWith this change the integration tests also pass with `ALLOW_CONSOLE=1`.\n\nFixes #343\n",
